{{- /*
  github/shared/pr-fetch-comments — retrieve every review comment, general PR
  comment, and review-thread for a PR/MR, then categorize the raw set for
  downstream triage/analysis.

  `gh pr view --json reviewThreads` does NOT exist — `reviewThreads` is a
  GraphQL-only field. This fragment fetches reviews + issue-level comments
  via `gh pr view --json reviews,comments` (both supported) and unresolved
  review threads via `gh api graphql` — replacing the mitto-emcc broken
  `gh pr view --json reviews,comments,reviewThreads` form previously
  inlined in `check-pr-comments` and `address-pr-comments`.

  Callers: check-pr-comments §2, address-pr-comments §2.

  Placeholders substituted by the agent from the surrounding context:
    <owner>/<repo> — the target repository (e.g. "some-org/some-repo")
    <number>       — the PR / MR number
*/ -}}
Retrieve every review comment, general PR comment, and unresolved review
thread. **Do not** use `gh pr view --json reviewThreads` — that field is
GraphQL-only and `gh pr view` will exit non-zero with `Unknown JSON field`.

```bash
# GitHub — reviews + issue-level PR comments (both are supported --json fields)
gh pr view <number> --json reviews,comments

# GitHub — unresolved (and not-outdated) review-thread comments (GraphQL only)
REPO_OWNER=$(echo "<owner>/<repo>" | cut -d/ -f1)
REPO_NAME=$(echo "<owner>/<repo>" | cut -d/ -f2)
gh api graphql -f query='
query($owner:String!,$name:String!,$number:Int!) {
  repository(owner:$owner, name:$name) {
    pullRequest(number:$number) {
      reviewThreads(first:100) { nodes {
        id isResolved isOutdated
        comments(first:20) { nodes {
          author { login } path line originalLine body createdAt
        } }
      } }
    }
  }
}' -F owner="$REPO_OWNER" -F name="$REPO_NAME" -F number=<number> \
  --jq '[.data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[]
         | select(.isResolved == false and .isOutdated == false)]'

# GitLab
glab mr view <number> --comments
```

Categorize the merged set into: review comments, inline code comments,
conversation threads, change requests, approvals-with-comments. **Ignore
threads you authored** and threads that are already marked resolved.
